  "description": "The Mexican Mafia (La eMe) is a predominantly Mexican-American prison gang founded in 1957 by Luis 'Huero Buff' Flores at Deuel Vocational Institution in Tracy, California, with no origins in Mexico. With an estimated 250–300 made members, it controls Sureño street gangs across Southern California through a tribute system, with over 50,000 affiliated street soldiers carrying out operations on the outside. Its primary rival is Nuestra Familia; it is allied with the Aryan Brotherhood. Membership is lifelong under a blood-in, blood-out oath.",
